## Dashboard

- Framework: **{% if dashboard_framework == "streamlit" %}Streamlit{% else %}Shiny for Python{% endif %}**. Changing it needs an ADR.
- Lives in `src/{{ module_name }}/app/`, installed by the `app` extra
  (`pip install {{ package_name }}[app]`).
- Start it with `make app`. It runs until stopped, so ask the developer first.
- Run its tests with `make app-test` (the `app` pytest marker).
{%- if dashboard_framework == "streamlit" %}
- Tested with `streamlit.testing.v1.AppTest`, which runs the script headlessly.
{%- else %}
- Server logic is unit-tested directly; browser flows use the Shiny Playwright
  controllers.
{%- endif %}
- The app holds no analysis logic. Every computation it shows comes from a
  public, tested function in `src/{{ module_name }}/`. A new feature is written
  and tested as a package function first, then wired into the app.
- Verify any visual change with a Playwright screenshot of the running app.

{% endif -%}
